# Of or relating to [[mesmerism]] or [[mesmerization]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1890|author={{w|Lafcadio Hearn}}|chapter=Karma|title=Karma and Other Stories and Essays|location=London|publisher={{w|George G. Harrap and Co.}}|year_published=1921|section=Chapter VI|oclc=1047481212|page=36|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/karmaotherstorie00hearuoft/page/36/mode/1up|passage=Even were he to write a lie, he could not meet her and maintain it, with her eyes upon his face: they had uttermost power over him—power as of life and death,—those fine grey sweet '''mesmeric''' eyes !}}
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Age of Consent|year=1962|page=152|passage=Podson's globular stare assured any woman that the bargain was sacred. It was solemn, intent, opaque; it was also slightly '''mesmeric''', which is to say that it gave out everything and took in nothing.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1938|author={{w|Xavier Herbert}}|chapter=VIII|title={{w|Capricornia (novel)|Capricornia}}|location=New York|publisher={{w|D. Appleton & Company|D. Appleton-Century Co., Inc.}}|year_published=1943|oclc=256094536|page=125|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/capricornianovel00herb/page/125/mode/1up|passage=Then suddenly he remembered something Differ had often talked about, what he called the Suggestive Power of the Written Word, the making, by means of arrangements of word and phrase, of '''mesmeric''' passes as it were before the reader's mind in order to convince—that was Differ's word, Convince!—Convince Against All Reason.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1990|author={{w|A.S. Byatt}}|title={{w|Possession (Byatt novel)|Possession: A Romance}}|chapter=6|page=113|publisher={{w|Random House}}|location=New York|isbn=9780394586236|oclc=1150994709|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/possessionromanc00byat/page/113/mode/1up|passage=She was a firm believer in '''mesmeric''' healing, from which she claimed to have benefited greatly, and she was also very much involved in the spiritualist experiments of those days {{...}}}}

